# fm84 as Gaeilge.
#
# Each msgid is the English as the code has it, and the msgstr under it what
# is shown in its place. A sentence with a count in it has a msgstr for each
# form the count takes: [one] for 1, [two] for 2, [few] for 3 to 6, [many]
# for 7 to 10 and [other] for the rest - "3 chomhad", "7 gcomhad", "20
# comhad". A msgctxt sets one use of a word apart from the same word
# elsewhere. {name} is a place the program fills, kept as it is. The keys
# to press - Y, N, A and the like - stay as they are.

